{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1480693-mages-as-reality-benders-for-a-scp-play","id":1480693,"title":"Mages as Reality Benders for a SCP play","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Mage: The Awakening"],"posts":[{"date":"2022-05-10T14:38:44-07:00","id":1480693,"title":"Mages as Reality Benders for a SCP play","content":"Hello!<br /> <br /> I'm storyteller on a SCP Chronicle I'm doing with Hunter. I'm very interested and really like the mechanics from the game, and it was a perfect introduction, now this players are on plays of proper Mage and Mummy, with a Chronicles of Darkness one being worked.<br /> <br /> But the SCP Chronicle still kicking and is the most loved, so after understand the system and their various forms, I'm starting to give mechanics to some things. I have in the works a freeform few-merits based Thaumaturgy, but that is more based on Vampires than anything. My real deal is Reality Benders and of course mages can be that. But I have a problem, a player wants to evolve into a reality bender [she purchases a lot of Supernatural Merits anyway and we all like the idea on paper], so I want some resemblance of <i>balance</i> but with a SCP fell instead of a mage.<br /> <br /> My ideas are the next, if something is not mention, that means it stays the same:<ul><li>&quot;Sleepers&quot; don't activate Paradox, reality benders are not affected by a Lie or natural order. <i>Reaching to much</i> creates Paradox, so do some gadgets that give Paradox die to any reality bender on the area.</li> <li>Reality Benders don't use some unnatural fuel, only willpower, instead of Mana Reality Benders use Willpower Points to do &quot;magic&quot;, their Maximum Willpower Points are increased by their Gnosis, and how many Willpower Points can be use on a &quot;spell&quot; are determined by Gnosis as Mana-per turn limits.</li> <li>Reality Benders don't use Rotes, not have Rote Skills. Praxis can be bought with any experience in exchange.</li> <li>Reality Benders don't use Yantra Tools, don't have dedicated tools neither. They still can use any other type of Yantra, High Speech being reskinned as the capacity to exteriorice will through voice.</li> <li>Reality Benders have Integrity and Breaking Points as normal mortal, but aren't affect by their own anomalous phenomena. Exposing someone to anomalous phenomena for selfish reasons is a Breaking Point with -2.</li> <li>Reality Benders can Counterspell <i>any</i> phenomena under the purview of their Arcana.</li> </ul>This are my ideas until now. About the path: as this is for only one player, I create a simple path based on the Supernatural Merits the player has: Ruling Arcana would be Forces and Spirit, and Inferior Arcana would be Life [because the player is very anti-biokinesis].<br /> <br /> Thanks and any advice is welcome. Sorry for any bad english, not first language.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27384-altidiya","name":"altidiya","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27384_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"39"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-05-11T04:22:00-07:00","id":1480738,"title":"","content":"Is a reality bender a specific thing from SCP or are you just using it as a broad term for the idea you're going for?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://theonyxpath.com/downloads/Backer%20Badge%20small.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/178-michael","name":"Michael","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar178_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3560"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-05-12T10:43:54-07:00","id":1480845,"title":"","content":"It sounds to me like they are becoming artificial Proximi due to an exposure to supernatural elements from various sources, mixed with tinkering with their occult Occult knowledge.<br /> <br /> Why not use their Gnosis pools as the size of their resource fuel ? One resource point recharges after a good night's sleep, same as Willpower. They can transform a Willpower point into a reality bending point on a one to one basis, but the reverse is not true. This way they get two resource points per rest (Willpower and Gnosis), without inflating their Willpower pool to levels that surpass the maximum of the main templates.<br /> <br /> In addition, you never specified how they interact with imbued items. Should Reality Bender be able to activate them with Willpower, then any one that gets one containing a Mind 3 healing of Willpower would probably be in a situation that gives them a comparable ability of improvisational power as a full mage. <br /> <br /> Regarding tools, you mentioned some gadgets give Paradox to all Reality Benders in the area. Then you mentioned they don't get tools or dedicated tools. So they get some weird variation of High Speech, concentration, oaths and purification, all which are very mage like. <br /> <br /> An alternative is to make it so they have an anomalous object linked to their powers, with some kind of Familiar bond. They need it to channel their abilities and it takes effort to to replace. Ether googles, a set of tarot cards, a box that creates origami birds or even a rifle forged of occult materials. Any purchased power would need to make sense for the tool they use to channel it. If it doesn't and they still try (like using the rifle for a healing spell), they get the same amount of Paradox as a non-free Reach.<br /> <br /> Lastly, I believe its important to specify if they can detect Clashes of Wills (since I didn't mention they get any variation of Mage Sight). Mages are the only splat that can, so long as they retain control of the concealing spell. This means that not only can they always spend Willpower on it, but even failing to pierce an effect, they know something odd is afoot. That is a huge advantage in their role as supernatural detectives.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>New experiences are the font of creativity, when seeking inspiration, break your routine.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1278855-the-agathos-kai-sophos-a-acanthus-legacy-of-strategists\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#1155CC\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">The Agathos Kai Sophos</span></span></a><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">, an Acanthus Legacy of strategists (Mind/Time)</span><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1360568-the-szary-stra%C5%BCnik-an-obrimos-legacy-of-scholars-of-the-glyphs-of-fate\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#1155CC\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">The Szary Stra\u017cnik</span></span></a><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">, an Obrimos Legacy whose invisible hands guide through the Glyphs of Fate (Fate/Prime)</span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24280-kaiserafini","name":"KaiserAfini","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24280_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2648"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-05-12T14:22:25-07:00","id":1480861,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Michael</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1480693-mages-as-reality-benders-for-a-scp-play?p=1480738#post1480738\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Is a reality bender a specific thing from SCP or are you just using it as a broad term for the idea you're going for?</div> </div> </div> </div>Within the SCP mythos, its a broad term for any anomalous entity or item that has such abilities. Its so broad that, at most it influences the threat level classification and may require the use of Scranton Reality Anchors as part of the special containment procedures.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>New experiences are the font of creativity, when seeking inspiration, break your routine.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1278855-the-agathos-kai-sophos-a-acanthus-legacy-of-strategists\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#1155CC\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">The Agathos Kai Sophos</span></span></a><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">, an Acanthus Legacy of strategists (Mind/Time)</span><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1360568-the-szary-stra%C5%BCnik-an-obrimos-legacy-of-scholars-of-the-glyphs-of-fate\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#1155CC\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">The Szary Stra\u017cnik</span></span></a><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">, an Obrimos Legacy whose invisible hands guide through the Glyphs of Fate (Fate/Prime)</span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24280-kaiserafini","name":"KaiserAfini","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24280_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2648"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-05-12T16:02:03-07:00","id":1480879,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Michael</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1480693-mages-as-reality-benders-for-a-scp-play?p=1480738#post1480738\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Is a reality bender a specific thing from SCP or are you just using it as a broad term for the idea you're going for?</div> </div> </div> </div>As mentioned, is a term on SCP that defines mostly people capable of alter reality on a fundamental level. They are varied and very capable, so mages is the most direct answer.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>KaiserAfini</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1480693-mages-as-reality-benders-for-a-scp-play?p=1480845#post1480845\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It sounds to me like they are becoming artificial Proximi due to an exposure to supernatural elements from various sources, mixed with tinkering with their occult Occult knowledge.</div> </div> </div> </div>Is a approximation, yeah!<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>KaiserAfini</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1480693-mages-as-reality-benders-for-a-scp-play?p=1480845#post1480845\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> Why not use their Gnosis pools as the size of their resource fuel ? One resource point recharges after a good night's sleep, same as Willpower. They can transform a Willpower point into a reality bending point on a one to one basis, but the reverse is not true. This way they get two resource points per rest (Willpower and Gnosis), without inflating their Willpower pool to levels that surpass the maximum of the main templates.</div> </div> </div> </div>I really like this idea. Thanks!<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>KaiserAfini</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1480693-mages-as-reality-benders-for-a-scp-play?p=1480845#post1480845\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> In addition, you never specified how they interact with imbued items. Should Reality Bender be able to activate them with Willpower, then any one that gets one containing a Mind 3 healing of Willpower would probably be in a situation that gives them a comparable ability of improvisational power as a full mage.</div> </div> </div> </div>I'm working and thinking on how interact with Attainments, this are the most magical but very useful. Imbued items and Rotecraft probably would be replaced for Legacy Attainments I see fit on the future.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>KaiserAfini</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1480693-mages-as-reality-benders-for-a-scp-play?p=1480845#post1480845\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> Regarding tools, you mentioned some gadgets give Paradox to all Reality Benders in the area. Then you mentioned they don't get tools or dedicated tools. So they get some weird variation of High Speech, concentration, oaths and purification, all which are very mage like.</div> </div> </div> </div>Concentration and variation High Speech can be very ad-hoc. Oaths and purification are very mage and my player never use it on Mage, so I forgot, but they are out aswell. <br /> <br /> About the gadgets, I was refering to external gadgets, as the Scranton Reality Anchors for example.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>KaiserAfini</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1480693-mages-as-reality-benders-for-a-scp-play?p=1480845#post1480845\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> An alternative is to make it so they have an anomalous object linked to their powers, with some kind of Familiar bond. They need it to channel their abilities and it takes effort to to replace. Ether googles, a set of tarot cards, a box that creates origami birds or even a rifle forged of occult materials. Any purchased power would need to make sense for the tool they use to channel it. If it doesn't and they still try (like using the rifle for a healing spell), they get the same amount of Paradox as a non-free Reach.</div> </div> </div> </div>I like this idea but more for a Storyteller SCP than for the player, they interact mostly with <i>living</i> SCPs than <i>anomalous </i><i>object.</i> Or maybe a type of &quot;Legacy&quot;.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>KaiserAfini</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1480693-mages-as-reality-benders-for-a-scp-play?p=1480845#post1480845\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Lastly, I believe its important to specify if they can detect Clashes of Wills (since I didn't mention they get any variation of Mage Sight). Mages are the only splat that can, so long as they retain control of the concealing spell. This means that not only can they always spend Willpower on it, but even failing to pierce an effect, they know something odd is afoot. That is a huge advantage in their role as supernatural detectives.</div> </div> </div> </div>My idea is this variant [player focused - human generalist reality bender a la SCP 239] can detect Clashes of Wills, giving a advantage the group don't have until now.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27384-altidiya","name":"altidiya","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27384_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"39"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-05-16T08:45:42-07:00","id":1481241,"title":"","content":"Would there be any specific flavor of reality bender you are looking into ? Magitech, shamans, something closer to the Department of Temporal Anomalies ? Perhaps a group that splintered from the Mysterium in order to explore the Emanation known as the Wanderer's Library ? <br /> <br /> The SCP Foundation itself could arguably be built by repurposing Task Force: Valkyrie or the Cheiron Group. Alternatively, you could take inspiration from Deviants: The Renegades, making the Foundation a conspiracy and the NPC a Devoted.<br /> <br /> If you are looking for a Legacy that can act as a generalist while maintaining the high tech supernatural science flavor of the SCP Foundation, then I think the <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/981289-2e-legacy-thaumatech-engineers\">Thaumatech Engineers</a> or the <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1402100-the-anima-meccanica-a-moros-legacy-of-entrepreneuring-inventors\">Anima Meccanica</a> might be able to fill that niche.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>New experiences are the font of creativity, when seeking inspiration, break your routine.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1278855-the-agathos-kai-sophos-a-acanthus-legacy-of-strategists\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#1155CC\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">The Agathos Kai Sophos</span></span></a><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">, an Acanthus Legacy of strategists (Mind/Time)</span><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1360568-the-szary-stra%C5%BCnik-an-obrimos-legacy-of-scholars-of-the-glyphs-of-fate\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#1155CC\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">The Szary Stra\u017cnik</span></span></a><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">, an Obrimos Legacy whose invisible hands guide through the Glyphs of Fate (Fate/Prime)</span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24280-kaiserafini","name":"KaiserAfini","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24280_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2648"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-05-23T16:31:23-07:00","id":1481798,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>altidiya</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1480693-mages-as-reality-benders-for-a-scp-play#post1480693\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">My ideas are the next, if something is not mention, that means it stays the same:<ul><li>&quot;Sleepers&quot; don't activate Paradox, reality benders are not affected by a Lie or natural order. <i>Reaching to much</i> creates Paradox, so do some gadgets that give Paradox die to any reality bender on the area.</li> <li>Reality Benders don't use some unnatural fuel, only willpower, instead of Mana Reality Benders use Willpower Points to do &quot;magic&quot;, their Maximum Willpower Points are increased by their Gnosis, and how many Willpower Points can be use on a &quot;spell&quot; are determined by Gnosis as Mana-per turn limits.</li> <li>Reality Benders don't use Rotes, not have Rote Skills. Praxis can be bought with any experience in exchange.</li> <li>Reality Benders don't use Yantra Tools, don't have dedicated tools neither. They still can use any other type of Yantra, High Speech being reskinned as the capacity to exteriorice will through voice.</li> <li>Reality Benders have Integrity and Breaking Points as normal mortal, but aren't affect by their own anomalous phenomena. Exposing someone to anomalous phenomena for selfish reasons is a Breaking Point with -2.</li> <li>Reality Benders can Counterspell <i>any</i> phenomena under the purview of their Arcana.</li> </ul>This are my ideas until now. About the path: as this is for only one player, I create a simple path based on the Supernatural Merits the player has: Ruling Arcana would be Forces and Spirit, and Inferior Arcana would be Life [because the player is very anti-biokinesis].</div> </div> </div> </div>I think some of your changes shouldn't be changes, just reflavored further for Type Greens. Keep in mind that while their powers are broad in scope and need nothing but will, it is also heavily impacted by their beliefs. Most Greens have practical limitations, weird techniques and so on based in personal belief, and even when they learn those aren't needed it doesn't make ditching them easy. Effects that truly have no such focus are almost universally unconscious actions:<ul><li>Mana as its own thing can represent the Green's confidence in their powers. You can adjust it or just reflavor methods of recharging to be ways to replenish this confidence;</li> <li>Rotes similarly work fine for them, as it focus their belief in how their power work;</li> <li>Same goes for Yantra Tools, especially because eliminating those Yantra will greatly de-power them.</li> </ul>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}